"                   sources=['minmax.c'],\n"
"                   include_dirs=[get_include()])\n"
"\n"
"setup(name='minmax', version='1.0', ext_modules=[minmax])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/c-info.reduction-loop-tutorial.rst:364
msgid ""
"After the above has been installed, it can be imported and used as follows. "
"Plain Python floats and ints work directly, thanks to the promoter. No "
"explicit ``np.float64(...)`` wrapping is needed::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/c-info.reduction-loop-tutorial.rst:368
msgid ""
">>> import numpy as np\n"
">>> import minmax\n"
">>> minmax.minimummaximum(3.0, 5.0)\n"
"(np.float64(3.0), np.float64(5.0))\n"
">>> minmax.minimummaximum(3, 5)\n"
"(np.float64(3.0), np.float64(5.0))\n"
">>> a = [3.0, 1.0, 4.0, 1.0, 5.0, 9.0, 2.0, 6.0]\n"
">>> minmax.minimummaximum.reduce(a)\n"
"(np.float64(1.0), np.float64(9.0))\n"
">>> b = np.array(a).reshape(2, 4)\n"
">>> minmax.minimummaximum.reduce(b, axis=None)\n"
"(np.float64(1.0), np.float64(9.0))\n"
">>> minmax.minimummaximum.reduce(b, axis=1)\n"
"(array([1., 2.]), array([4., 9.]))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/c-info.reduction-loop-tutorial.rst:383
msgid ""
"Note that ``minimummaximum.reduce`` returns a tuple with one array per "
"output, rather than a single array, so it is usually unpacked as ``lo, hi = "
"minimummaximum.reduce(a)``. The ``initial`` argument of a multi-output "
"``reduce`` accepts either a single scalar, which seeds every output, or a "
"tuple with one value per output. The entries of such a tuple cannot be "
"``None``; a plain ``initial=None`` still unsets the initial value for the "
"whole reduction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/c-info.reduction-loop-tutorial.rst:392
msgid "Limitations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/c-info.reduction-loop-tutorial.rst:394
msgid ""
"This example is intentionally minimal and leaves out several things a real-"
"world implementation, like the built-in :func:`numpy.add` or a fuller "
"``minimummaximum``, would normally have:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/c-info.reduction-loop-tutorial.rst:398
msgid ""
"The promoter always resolves to ``'f8'``, regardless of the input dtypes. "
"Integer input arrays are therefore silently cast to ``float64`` instead of "
"keeping their own dtype. A multi-dtype ufunc would register a loop per dtype "
"and pick the common one, as the built-in :func:`numpy.minimum`/:func:`numpy."
"maximum` do."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/c-info.reduction-loop-tutorial.rst:403
msgid ""
"It registers no reduction identity. Reducing an empty array therefore raises "
"a :exc:`ValueError`, the same as ``numpy.maximum.reduce``. A multi-output "
"ufunc can provide per-output identities with the :c:macro:"
"`NPY_METH_get_multi_reduction_initials` slot, the multi-output version of :c:"
"macro:`NPY_METH_get_reduction_initial`. Its function fills one initial value "
"per output, for example ``+inf`` for the running minimum and ``-inf`` for "
"the running maximum. Reducing an empty array, or reducing with a ``where=`` "
"mask, then returns those identities instead of raising::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/c-info.reduction-loop-tutorial.rst:412
msgid ""
"static int\n"
"minimummaximum_get_multi_reduction_initials(\n"
"        PyArrayMethod_Context *NPY_UNUSED(context),\n"
"        npy_bool NPY_UNUSED(reduction_is_empty), void **initials)\n"
"{\n"
"    *(double *)initials[0] = NPY_INFINITY;   /* min identity */\n"
"    *(double *)initials[1] = -NPY_INFINITY;  /* max identity */\n"
"    return 1;\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/c-info.reduction-loop-tutorial.rst:422
msgid ""
"It is registered alongside the reduction loop, by adding this entry to the "
"``slots`` array above: ``{NPY_METH_get_multi_reduction_initials, (void "
"*)&minimummaximum_get_multi_reduction_initials}``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/c-info.reduction-loop-tutorial.rst:425
msgid ""
":meth:`~numpy.ufunc.accumulate`, :meth:`~numpy.ufunc.reduceat`, and :meth:"
"`~numpy.ufunc.at` are not supported for multi-output ufuncs yet, only :meth:"
"`~numpy.ufunc.reduce` is."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/c-info.reduction-loop-tutorial.rst:431
msgid ""
":doc:`ArrayMethod API reference </reference/c-api/array>` for the full :c:"
"macro:`NPY_METH_get_reduction_loop` reference documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/c-info.reduction-loop-tutorial.rst:433
msgid ""
":ref:`ufuncs-basics` for the Python-level behavior of :meth:`~numpy.ufunc."
"reduce` on multi-output ufuncs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/c-info.reduction-loop-tutorial.rst:7
msgid "ufunc"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/c-info.reduction-loop-tutorial.rst:7
msgid "reduction"
msgstr ""
